  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central America SAIs&apos; Institutional capacities development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant would continue the Bank&apos;s support to the Central American Organization of Supreme Audit Institutions (OCCEFS), building up on its successful ongoing partnership, while recognizing the inherent long term/continuous improvement nature of public financial accountability reforms. The grant would have as development objectives: (i) to strengthen the capacity of OCCEFS members to improve institutional capabilities through enhance their  knowledge sharing  and training capacity taking advantage of regional best practices with technology based mechanisms for establishing a long distance knowledge learning network  on financial accountability matters; and (ii) to strengthen the capacity of OCCEFS members to higher quality and competences qualification through a common regional curricula and potentially agreed on common certification standard for public sector auditor.</narrative>
  </description>
